# Optional environment for wmr-bridge.service.
# Copy to /etc/wmr-bridge/wmr-bridge.env (or let pi/install.sh create it).
#
# Pass extra CLI flags without editing the systemd unit. The default is empty;
# systemd expands the value into ExecStart, and an unset variable makes systemd
# warn on every start.
WMR_BRIDGE_ARGS=""
#
# For example, single-hand mode on a dedicated Pi:
# WMR_BRIDGE_ARGS="--hand left"
#
# Onboard serial/UART Bluetooth (hci_uart) auto-disables BLE GATT at startup
# and runs TCP-only. To force BLE GATT on a serial/UART adapter:
# WMR_BRIDGE_ARGS="--ble-allow-serial"
#
# Controller idle policy: the bridge keeps streaming while buttons, sticks,
# trigger or gyro move. After 5 min without activity it pauses the 10 s 0x06
# keep-alive so the controller can sleep; after 15 min it disconnects Bluetooth
# so the controller powers off. 0 disables either stage, and the power-off
# timeout must be 0 or at least the sleep timeout. To tune both stages:
# WMR_BRIDGE_ARGS="--idle-sleep-timeout 300 --idle-poweroff-timeout 900"
#
# The unit passes --token-file /etc/wmr-bridge/token. That file must be owned by
# the service user (chown wmr:wmr, mode 640), otherwise the daemon cannot read
# it and systemd restarts it. The wmr group can read it, so add an admin who
# runs pi/tools/wifi_probe.py to that group. To use an environment variable
# instead, remove --token-file from ExecStart and set:
# WMR_BRIDGE_TOKEN=change-me
#
# Never commit a real token.
